---
name: akka-aspire-implementation
description: Parallel implementation of Akka.NET Aspire hosting plugin packages
version: 1.0
---

# Phase 2: Implement three core packages in parallel, then verify

agent redis-impl:
  model: sonnet
  prompt: """
You are implementing the Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis package - a Redis-based service discovery plugin for Akka.NET modeled after Akka.Discovery.Azure.

Read these reference files to understand the patterns:
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/AzureServiceDiscovery.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/ClusterMemberTableClient.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/AzureDiscoverySettings.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/AzureDiscoveryOptions.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/AkkaHostingExtensions.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/Actors/AzureDiscoveryGuardian.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/Actors/HeartbeatActor.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/olympus/Akka.Management/src/discovery/azure/Akka.Discovery.Azure/reference.conf
"""

agent hosting-impl:
  model: sonnet
  prompt: """
You are implementing the Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting package - an Orleans-style AppHost integration for Akka.NET in .NET Aspire.

Read these reference files to understand the patterns being extracted:
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/petabridge/sdkbin/src/Sdkbin.AppHost/AkkaManagementExtensions.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/petabridge/DrawTogether.NET/src/DrawTogether.AppHost/AkkaManagementExtensions.cs
"""

agent client-impl:
  model: sonnet
  prompt: """
You are implementing the Aaron.Akka.Aspire package - the client/service-side Akka.NET Aspire cluster bootstrap.

Read these reference files to understand the configuration patterns:
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/petabridge/DrawTogether.NET/src/DrawTogether/Config/AkkaConfiguration.cs
- /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/petabridge/sdkbin/src/Sdkbin.AppHost/AkkaManagementExtensions.cs
"""

# Run all three implementations in parallel
parallel:
  redis = session: redis-impl
    prompt: """
Implement the Redis discovery plugin at /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/src/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis/.

The reference.conf already exists. Create/replace these files:

1. RedisDiscoverySettings.cs - Immutable settings class modeled after AzureDiscoverySettings. Properties: ServiceName, HostName, Port, ConnectionString, Ttl (TimeSpan, default 2m), TtlHeartbeatInterval (TimeSpan, default 30s), KeyPrefix (string, default "akka:discovery"). Include factory method Create(ActorSystem) and Create(Config) that reads from HOCON. Include fluent With*() copy methods.

2. RedisDiscoveryOptions.cs - Akka.Hosting options class implementing IDiscoveryOptions. Modeled after AzureDiscoveryOptions. Has nullable properties for all settings. Apply() generates HOCON config and adds it to builder.

3. ClusterMemberRedisClient.cs - Internal class managing Redis operations. Uses StackExchange.Redis.IDatabase. Key format: {keyPrefix}:{serviceName}:{host}:{port} with value as JSON. Methods: GetOrCreateAsync, GetAllAsync (use SCAN not KEYS), UpdateAsync, RemoveSelf. Accept IConnectionMultiplexer in constructor.

4. Actors/RedisDiscoveryGuardian.cs - Guardian actor modeled after AzureDiscoveryGuardian. State machine: Initializing -> Running -> Stopping. Creates HeartbeatActor child. Handles Lookup and StopDiscovery messages.

5. Actors/HeartbeatActor.cs - Periodic heartbeat actor using IWithTimers for TTL refresh.

6. RedisDiscovery.cs - IExtension class providing DefaultConfiguration() loading embedded reference.conf.

7. RedisServiceDiscovery.cs - Replace placeholder. Extends Akka.Discovery.ServiceDiscovery. Creates guardian actor, handles Lookup, registers CoordinatedShutdown task.

8. AkkaHostingExtensions.cs - Extension methods: WithRedisDiscovery(connectionString, ...) and WithRedisDiscovery(Action<RedisDiscoveryOptions>).

Important: Use #nullable enable for netstandard2.0 compatibility. Namespace: Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis (and .Actors for actors). Use System.Text.Json for serialization.

Then write tests in /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/tests/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis.Tests/:
- RedisDiscoverySettingsSpecs.cs - Test HOCON parsing and settings creation
- HostingSpecs.cs - Test WithRedisDiscovery() generates correct HOCON config
Delete PlaceholderTest.cs when you add real tests.

Verify: dotnet build src/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis.csproj
And: dotnet test tests/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis.Tests/Aaron.Akka.Discovery.Redis.Tests.csproj
"""

  hosting = session: hosting-impl
    prompt: """
Implement the Aspire hosting package at /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/src/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting/.

Create these files:

1. IClusteringProvider.cs - Interface with ConfigureResource<T>(IResourceBuilder<T> builder) where T : IResourceWithEnvironment.

2. ClusteringProvider.cs - Internal implementation. Auto-detects provider type by stripping "Resource" suffix from resource type name. Calls builder.WithReference(resource) for connection string. Sets Akka__Cluster__Clustering__ProviderType env var.

3. AkkaService.cs - Replace placeholder. Config holder class with Name, Builder (IDistributedApplicationBuilder), and Clustering (IClusteringProvider?) properties.

4. AkkaServiceExtensions.cs - Extension methods:
   - AddAkka(this IDistributedApplicationBuilder, string name) -> returns AkkaService
   - WithClustering(this AkkaService, IResourceBuilder<IResourceWithConnectionString>) -> sets clustering provider
   - WithReference<T>(this IResourceBuilder<T>, AkkaService) where T : IResourceWithEnvironment, IResourceWithEndpoints
     This method: calls Clustering.ConfigureResource, adds TCP endpoints "akka-remote" and "akka-management" (isProxied: true, scheme: "tcp"), sets env vars (Akka__Cluster__Enabled=true, PublicHostName=localhost, ServiceName, FilterOnFallbackPort=false, RequiredContactPointsNr from replica annotations).

Namespace: Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting

Write tests in /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting.Tests/:
- AkkaServiceExtensionsSpecs.cs - Test AddAkka, WithClustering, WithReference
Delete PlaceholderTest.cs when you add real tests.

Verify: dotnet build src/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting.csproj
And: dotnet test tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting.Tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Hosting.Tests.csproj
"""

  client = session: client-impl
    prompt: """
Implement the client package at /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/src/Aaron.Akka.Aspire/.

Create these files:

1. AkkaDiscoveryMethod.cs - Enum: Redis, AzureTableStorage, Kubernetes, Config

2. AkkaAspireClusterSettings.cs - Replace placeholder. Settings POCO bound from Akka:Cluster: config section. Properties: Enabled (bool, false), RemotePort (int, 8081), ManagementPort (int, 8558), PublicHostName (string, localhost), ServiceName (string, default), RequiredContactPointsNr (int, 1), FilterOnFallbackPort (bool, false), Clustering (AkkaAspireClusteringSettings? with ProviderType string?).

3. AkkaAspireExtensions.cs - Extension method WithAspireClusterBootstrap(this AkkaConfigurationBuilder, IServiceProvider sp, Action<ClusterOptions>? clusterConfigure = null). Reads settings from IConfiguration Akka:Cluster section. If Enabled=false, no-op. Otherwise configures: Akka.Remote (bind 0.0.0.0, advertise PublicHostName:RemotePort), Clustering (clear seed nodes, apply callback), Akka.Management HTTP, Cluster Bootstrap (RequiredContactPointsNr, FilterOnFallbackPort, StableMargin=5s, ServiceName), discovery method from ProviderType, health checks.

Namespace: Aaron.Akka.Aspire

Write tests in /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Tests/:
- AkkaAspireClusterSettingsSpecs.cs - Test settings binding from IConfiguration
- AkkaAspireExtensionsSpecs.cs - Test WithAspireClusterBootstrap (no-op when disabled, configures when enabled)
Delete PlaceholderTest.cs when you add real tests.

Verify: dotnet build src/Aaron.Akka.Aspire/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.csproj
And: dotnet test tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Tests/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.Tests.csproj
"""

# After all parallel streams complete, verify the full solution
session "Verify all packages build and test together. Run: dotnet build /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.slnx && dotnet test /home/aaronontheweb/repositories/stannardlabs/akka.net-aspire-plugin/Aaron.Akka.Aspire.slnx. If there are failures, read the errors, fix the source files, and re-run until green."
  context: { redis, hosting, client }
